  "review": {
    "review": "The hero died after prolonged caster and skeleton pressure. Decision 3555's accepted transition (log line 10376) reduces HP from five to zero during a wand attack; the exact damage source is not established. An earlier selecting defect is supported: decisions 3486, 3490 and 3492 approach a visible necromancer while below half health, keeping contact with its skeleton. At 3490, the approach loses health and is immediately reversed by retreat at 3491, before being repeated at 3492. The necromancer helper vetoed wounded contact approaches only for remembered casters, not visible ones. Independent public-observation helper probes reproduce these original choices; they are not recovered whole-run memory. A focused correction extends the existing veto to visible-caster approaches while retaining immediate admitted caster attacks and existing withdrawal checks. The new regression fails on the original policy and passes on the candidate; the full suite passes 2,041 tests with four skipped. This establishes a local selection repair, not survival, a confirmed killer, or a successful counterfactual escape. Changed files are supplied through the trusted adapter.",
    "learnings": "Seeing a support caster does not justify wounded movement beside its minion. Keep immediate admitted caster attacks available, but prefer existing contact-free withdrawal over exposed approach steps. A spacing choice alone does not prove lasting safety."
